    "result_text": "The build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag that is `true` when an owner's city already holds between 40 and 49 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), following the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the Owner schema (drives the generated `OwnerDto`; MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `capacityWarning` field with a `capacity_warning` column plus getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Captured the city owner count into `ownersInCity` (reusing it for the unchanged `>= 50` hard rejection), and set `owner.setCapacityWarning(ownersInCity >= 40 && ownersInCity < 50)` alongside the other derived flags.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 Added the `capacity_warning` column.\n\nThe `>= 50` hard rejection is untouched. The full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, the only test present) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
